WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.880
Do violent video games lead to violence?
暴力电子游戏会导致暴力吗？

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:12.260
Many studies suggest that violent video games may make children more aggressive in real life.
许多研究表明，暴力电子游戏可能会让孩子在现实生活中更具攻击性。

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:22.430
In my opinion, although such games alone seldom turn a person violent, they can indeed encourage aggressive behavior, especially among young players.
在我看来，虽然这类游戏本身很少会让一个人变得暴力，但它们确实会助长攻击性行为，在年轻玩家中尤其如此。

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.470
Children are still developing their sense of right and wrong.
孩子们的是非观仍在形成之中。

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:36.170
When they spend hours playing games in which fighting and killing are rewarded with points, they may come to see violence as an acceptable way to solve problems.
当他们花几个小时玩那些打斗和杀戮能得分的游戏时，他们可能会逐渐把暴力看作解决问题的一种可以接受的方式。

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.430
Some may even copy the foul language and violent actions they see on the screen.
有些孩子甚至会模仿他们在屏幕上看到的脏话和暴力动作。

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:48.110
Moreover, playing such games for long periods can make players less sensitive to the suffering of others.
此外，长时间玩这类游戏会让玩家对他人的痛苦变得不那么敏感。

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:57.580
Of course, violence has many causes, such as family problems and peer pressure, and not everyone who plays these games becomes violent.
当然，暴力有很多成因，比如家庭问题和同伴压力，而且并不是每个玩这些游戏的人都会变得暴力。

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.310
Still, the risks cannot be ignored.
尽管如此，这些风险不容忽视。

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:10.020
Parents should choose games suitable for their children’s age and limit their playing time, and game companies should take their social responsibility seriously.
家长应当选择适合孩子年龄的游戏，并限制他们玩游戏的时间；游戏公司也应当认真承担起自己的社会责任。

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.470
With such measures, young people can enjoy games without being harmed by them.
有了这些措施，年轻人就能享受游戏，而不会受到游戏的伤害。
